I finished T25 and T26 and mostly finished T27. The run stopped there, so T28 onward is not started. I did not run the wave-end code review, so the review findings below are my own.

| Task | Status | Tests added | Verification | Commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| T25 `POST /api/runs` | [x] done | 9 `pg_` tests and 2 non-database tests (`validation_rejects_without_side_effects`, `validation_errors_use_the_documented_status`) | fmt, clippy `-D warnings`, workspace tests and the server `pg_` tests all passed | `e1ef27d` |
| T26 `GET /api/runs/{id}` | [x] done | 4 `pg_` tests | same gate, all passed | `c2b4e50` |
| T27 `POST /api/runs/{id}/cancel` | [ ] partial | 5 tests, 4 of them `pg_` (the sixth is non-database) | same gate, all passed | `0e1944e` |

Notes on the work:

- **T25:** A replayed request returns before any rate limit is counted. The per-IP key is read from `X-Forwarded-For` only when the socket address is in `TRUSTED_PROXIES`. I added a `client_ip` module for that, and `main` now serves with connect info.
- **T26:** A missing, malformed or foreign run returns the same `404` body, and the test checks that. Sample details are copied through a three-field whitelist. Timestamps are formatted in SQL, so I did not add the sqlx `time` feature.
- **T27:** The endpoint only sets the cancel flag and sends a wake-up. The queued-cancel test runs the real judge claim, and the executor never runs. Two named tests are missing: `pg_cancel_running` and `pg_cancel_never_yields_both_done_and_error`. Both need a live claim with a heartbeat, and the test setting for the renewal interval is not in the spec. I left T27 unticked.
- **Database:** I ran the `pg_` tests against a throwaway `postgres:17-alpine` with a password typed inline. The container is stopped and no credential was written to a file. Valkey was not needed, because these tests use the in-memory limiter.
- **No hooks blocked a write this run.** Every edit went through the file tools.

**Blockers:** written to `docs/kiro-log/run-lifecycle-blockers.md`. The entry covers the two missing T27 tests and the choices made in T25 and T26.

**Review queue:** nothing this pass. T25, T26 and T27 are not `[SUPERVISED]`.

**Open Minor findings for the hand-off:**
- `ConnectInfo` is required by `POST /api/runs` and cancel, so any router served without connect info returns `500`. Only `main` and the test support build it that way today.
- The trusted-proxy logic handles IPv4 only. An IPv6 peer is never trusted.
- `queue_cap` and `queue_full` send `retry_after_seconds: 1`, the minimum the requirements allow. Nothing better was specified.

**Next step:** finish T27's two tests, then start T28 (`RunWaker`).
